Flips
When a player dies, they flip their role card, revealing their role to all. If somebody is killed during the night, the flips will happen in the morning when everyone wakes up. If somebody dies during the day, they will immediately flip their card. If a Reporter (see elections) is in play, there are no flips and the cards of dead players are not revealed.
Card Mix
Players can use whatever character card mix they agree upon. That being said, the best way to learn how to play is to use the following basic ratios:
8-11 Players: 2 Werewolves, 1 Seer + Other Townsfolk
12-17 Players: 3 Werewolves, 1 Seer + Other Townsfolk
18+ Players: 4 Werewolves, 1 Seer + Other Townsfolk
If all players are already familiar with the game you should start by adding some of the other basic characters. After a while, you may want to move to adding some of the intermediate and advanced roles listed from Page 17 onwards. If you decide to add more powerful Townsfolk roles, you should also compensate by adding more or stronger Werewolf roles.
